LOCATED FIX SITE(S) — traced in this repository before you were asked. Anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces:
- src/services/contentstack.ts :: options — This is the Stack configuration site — the single contentstack.Stack(options) call at line 91 that every data fetch flows through (via ContentstackFactory). The options object (lines 71-89) currently contains api_key, delivery_token, environment, branch, fetchOptions but NO live_preview block. Adding live_preview here is what enables the SDK to detect preview mode and return draft entries — without it, no downstream consumer can ever receive preview data.
- src/pages/_app.tsx :: ContentstackContext.Provider — This is the app-wide provider site where ContentstackContext.Provider wraps the application and sets the context value from server-side page props (header, footer, onboarding, page). For live preview, @contentstack/live-preview-utils must be initialized here with an onEntryChange callback that receives updated entry data from the CMS and pushes it into React state, causing the provider value and all 147+ useContent consumers to re-render. This callback is the PRODUCER of live preview entry data on the client.
- src/context/contentstackContext.tsx :: ContentstackContext — The React context that distributes Contentstack data to all components via the useContent hook. Currently createContext<IContentstackContext>({}) with a static interface — the Provider value is set once from server-side props and never updated. For live preview, this context must CARRY reactive state so that when onEntryChange in _app.tsx fires with updated entry data, all useContent consumers re-render with new values.
- src/components/pages/Homepage.tsx :: Homepage — Target page per acceptance criteria (MX Homepage). Receives page prop (IContentstackPage[]) and renders ContentStackHomePageHeroBanner, HomepageComponentMapper, ContentstackRecentNews, ContentStackLandAcknowledgement. Child components use useContent hook which reads from ContentstackContext. Once the context becomes reactive via onEntryChange, Homepage and all its children will automatically re-render with preview data — no direct edit needed.
- src/services/pageService.ts :: PageService.getPageEntry — Server-side data fetcher (lines 166-229) that populates the page prop passed to ContentstackContext.Provider. Calls getSinglePageEntry (line 211) or getSingletonPageEntry (line 212) which delegate to getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry from contentstack.ts. This is the existing server-side pipeline that live preview augments client-side. The getSinglePageEntry function (line 75-88) uses getSingleEntry with contentstackConfig lookup — this same pattern should be reused in the onEntryChange callback for client-side re-fetching of preview entries.


